From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:31:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 139/342] meson_decoder: HEVC

The plugin takes what FFmpeg's reader calls HEVC too, when its first
sequence parameter set says 4:2:0, 8 or 10 bits, up to 1920x1088: the
hvcC record's parameter sets go ahead of the stream, its length-prefixed
NAL units become Annex B ones. Frames start where the driver says
(meson_vdec_frame.offset), and the clones of the driver's frame areas
are kept per area.

On the ODROID-C2, MediaPlayer plays 1080p30 8-bit and 10-bit and 1080p60
HEVC without dropped frames at 8-25% CPU; FFmpeg can't play the 10-bit
or the 1080p60 one. Seeks and moving through a playlist keep the
hardware decoder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
